  "releaseNotes": "﻿### Changed\n- Core is ready for a second language server: `.ai/commands.json` reads each language's section on its own, so a `node` section (`enabled`, `packages`, `testScript`, `coverageScript`, `coverageFile`, `timeoutMinutes`) or a `python` section no longer makes the .NET server ignore the whole file, and a bad section only voids that language's settings; `COVERAGE.md` sections are per language (`.NET`, `Node`), a missing one is inserted in the documented order (.NET, Node, Python, Shell), and a section is written under an exclusive lock so two servers finishing together keep both sections; the repository watcher takes a watch plan (exact file names, recursive or not, which directories), so a Node server can watch a few directories without one kernel watch per `node_modules` directory. The .NET server's tools, schemas and figures are unchanged (#37)",
